  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Positive Masculinity Project EECA (UNAIDS-UNESCO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNAIDS and UNESCO IITE initiate this joint project with an aim to build positive masculinities, create non-violent environment and address the issue of violence, including GBV in Armenia. The project will primarily target adolescent boys and young men aged 16-25 as agents of positive change. Key activities include: (1) measurement of the level of anxiety and attitudes towards violence and GBV among young men, (2) development and promotion of educational materials to transform harmful norms, attitudes and reduce GBV, (3) development and promotion of a communication campaign in social media with the engagement of celebrities to reach wider audience and amplify the key messages of zero tolerance to violence/GBV. It is expected that over 200,000 people will be reached by the campaign.</narrative>
  </description>
